<title>PHILIPPINES: MANILA'S PHIBOR RISE ACROSS ALL MATURITIES.</title>
<headline>MANILA'S PHIBOR RISE ACROSS ALL MATURITIES.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) inched higher across all maturities on Wednesday after the peso came under fresh pressure in tandem with other regional currencies, traders said.</p>
<p>&quot;The view now is that interest rates will stay high,&quot; a foreign bank trader said.</p>
<p>Banks had previously expected interest rates to decline after the peso exhibited relative strength last week.</p>
<p>PHIBOR is the average swap quotes given by 20 banks operating in the country.</p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			  AUG 13		 AUG 12</p>
<p>    1 W		18  1/2		 18  1/4</p>
<p>    2 W		18  1/8		 17  3/4</p>
<p>    1 M		18  1/8		 17  5/16</p>
<p>    2 M		17  5/16		16  9/16</p>
<p>    3 M		16  7/8		 16  5/16</p>
<p>    6 M		17			16  7/16</p>
<p>    12M		16  7/16		15 15/16</p>
<p>    VAL		14-Aug		  13-Aug</p>
